==== NAME
libpdx-volume — KIND_VOLUME client helpers, PDXB superblock codec, and
mount-table view for paideia-os volume tooling.

==== SYNOPSIS
    module VolKind = structure {
      pub let vol_kind_mint   : (u64) -> u64 !{} @{}
      pub let vol_kind_narrow : (u64, u64, u64) -> u64 !{mem} @{}
    }
    module PdxbSuperblock = structure {
      pub let pdxb_parse_superblock  : (u64, u64, u64) -> u64 !{mem} @{}
      pub let pdxb_encode_superblock : (u64, u64, u64) -> u64 !{mem} @{}
    }
    module MountTable = structure {
      pub let mount_table_row_parse : (u64, u64) -> u64 !{mem} @{}
    }
    module MountTableSnapshot = structure {
      pub let mount_table_snapshot : (u64, u64, u64, u64) -> u64 !{mem} @{}
    }
    module PdxbSign = structure {
      pub let pdxb_sign_superblock   : (u64, u64, u64, u64) -> u64 !{mem, crypto} @{paideia.crypto}
      pub let pdxb_sign_inode_tail   : (u64, u64, u64, u64, u64) -> u64 !{mem, crypto} @{paideia.crypto}
      pub let pdxb_verify_inode_tail : (u64, u64, u64, u64, u64, u64) -> u64 !{} @{}
    }

==== DESCRIPTION
libpdx-volume is the single shared client-side library `mkfs.pdxfs`,
`mount.pdxfs`, and `umount.pdxfs` (and, later, `df` / `fsck.pdxfs`) all
link, so the on-disk PDXB wire format and the `KIND_PDXFS_MOUNT_TABLE`
row layout are decoded and encoded in exactly one place rather than
once per tool. It performs no `sys_svc_lookup` of its own and binds no
ambient service at process start — every public entry point takes a
caller-supplied capability slot or raw pointer as a plain `u64`
argument and operates against a KIND surface the CALLER already holds
(see `caps.decl`'s closing note). The library issues **zero cap-invoke
syscalls anywhere in its own call graph**, at every milestone through
v1.0.0.

Five modules cover three concerns:

- **`VolKind`** — thin wrappers over `KIND_VOLUME` mint/narrow so a
  caller never hand-packs a mint/narrow call's arguments.
- **`PdxbSuperblock`** — the PDXB v1 on-disk 4096-byte superblock
  codec: the single place that wire format is decoded/encoded.
- **`MountTable`** / **`MountTableSnapshot`** — the client-side view of
  the `KIND_PDXFS_MOUNT_TABLE` capability's singleton metadata row, and
  the live per-mount-entry array it points at.
- **`PdxbSign`** — ML-DSA-65 signing helpers over a superblock or an
  inode-tail byte range, via the paideia-as `MlDsa65::sign` intrinsic.

See [[cref: WIRE-FORMATS]] for both on-wire byte layouts this library
decodes, [[cref: API]] for the full per-function contract, and
[[cref: LIMITATIONS]] for what is stubbed or deferred at v1.0.0.

==== API

---- vol_kind_mint(dev_cap) -> vol_cap
**STUB.** Always returns `LPV_STUB_NOT_IMPLEMENTED`. Blocked on a
ring-3-reachable `KIND_VOLUME` mint syscall that does not exist yet
(`kind_volume.pdx`'s own "no cap-invoke op reaches kind_volume_mint"
note). Dereferences nothing.

---- vol_kind_narrow(cap_slot, requested_ops_mask, out_narrowed_cap_slot) -> err
Validates `requested_ops_mask` against `KIND_VOLUME`'s real, frozen op
catalog — ordinals 0..9, `VK_OPS_VALID_MASK = 0x3FF`. On a valid mask,
writes `cap_slot` through to `*out_narrowed_cap_slot` **unchanged**
(documented passthrough, not a kernel-enforced derivation — no
`cap_narrow` primitive exists anywhere in the kernel tree for
`KIND_VOLUME`) and returns `LPV_VK_OK` (0). On an invalid mask, returns
`LPV_VK_ERR_BAD_OPS_MASK` (1) and does not write `out_narrowed_cap_slot`.

CAUTION: this function's real value is the validation gate, not
capability narrowing. A caller expecting a genuinely narrower
capability back gets the same `cap_slot` it passed in.

---- pdxb_parse_superblock(buf_ptr, buf_len, out_ptr) -> err
Decodes a 4096-byte on-disk PDXB v1 superblock buffer at `buf_ptr` into
a 176-byte `PdxbSuperblockSummary` at `out_ptr` (see
[[cref: WIRE-FORMATS]]). Four gates, checked in order:
`buf_len >= 4096` (`PDXB_ERR_BUF_TOO_SHORT`), `magic == PDXB_MAGIC`
(`PDXB_ERR_BAD_MAGIC`), `version == 1` (`PDXB_ERR_BAD_VERSION`),
`block_size == 4096` (`PDXB_ERR_BAD_BLOCK_SIZE`). Returns `PDXB_OK` (0)
on success. There is no on-disk checksum field to validate against —
the on-disk PDXB v1 layout has none; `block_size` is the closest real
substitute per `design/architecture.md` §3.1.

---- pdxb_encode_superblock(sb_ptr, out_ptr, out_len) -> written_or_err
Inverse of `pdxb_parse_superblock`: reads a `PdxbSuperblockSummary` at
`sb_ptr` and writes the full 4096-byte on-disk layout to `out_ptr`.
Zero-fills the entire output buffer first, then overlays all eighteen
real fields — `_reserved` and `sig` are left at their zeroed state (no
signature is produced here; see `pdxb_sign_superblock`). Returns
`out_len` (4096) on success, `PDXB_ENC_ERR_BUF_TOO_SHORT` if the
caller's buffer is smaller than 4096 bytes.

---- mount_table_row_parse(row_ptr, out_ptr) -> err
Decodes the 64-byte `KIND_PDXFS_MOUNT_TABLE` singleton capability
metadata row at `row_ptr` into a 56-byte `MountTableRow` at `out_ptr`
(see [[cref: WIRE-FORMATS]]). Two gates: the row's `kind` field must
equal `0x1A5` (`LPV_MTR_ERR_BAD_MAGIC`, 1), and its `in_use` byte must
be nonzero (`LPV_MTR_ERR_ROW_DEAD`, 2). Returns `LPV_MTR_OK` (0) on
success. This row has no separate version field — `kind` is its only
discriminator.

---- mount_table_snapshot(row_ptr, out_ptr, out_cap, out_count_ptr) -> err
Re-validates the same singleton row as `mount_table_row_parse` (same
two gates, same two error codes, `LPV_MTS_OK` / `LPV_MTS_ERR_BAD_MAGIC`
/ `LPV_MTS_ERR_ROW_DEAD`), then walks the LIVE `_mount_table[8]`
per-slot array the row's `table_row_addr` field points at, decoding up
to `out_cap` entries into `out_ptr` and writing the number actually
written (`min(mount_slot_count, out_cap)`) to `*out_count_ptr`. The
walk is unconditional over the slot range — empty slots are decoded
and written too; a caller wanting only live mounts filters by the
decoded `flags` field's bit 0 (`MOUNT_FLAG_VALID`) itself.

---- pdxb_sign_superblock(sb_ptr, seed_ptr, out_sig_ptr, out_sig_len) -> written_or_err
Signs `sb_ptr[0, 696)` (the wire format's documented signed range,
[[cref: WIRE-FORMATS]]) via the paideia-as `MlDsa65::sign` intrinsic
using the 32-byte seed at `seed_ptr`, and writes the 3309-byte
signature to `out_sig_ptr`. Pass `out_sig_ptr = sb_ptr + 696` to sign
in place, matching the on-disk `sig` field's own offset. Returns
`3309` on success, `PDXB_SIGN_ERR` if the intrinsic call fails. Takes a
raw `seed_ptr` rather than a `KIND_SIG_KEY` cap slot — see
[[cref: LIMITATIONS]].

---- pdxb_sign_inode_tail(inode_ptr, tail_offset, tail_len, seed_ptr, out_sig_ptr) -> written_or_err
Same signing path as `pdxb_sign_superblock`, over an arbitrary
`inode_ptr[tail_offset, tail_offset + tail_len)` byte range instead of
a fixed superblock prefix. Deferred consumer — no `fsck.pdxfs` exists
yet to call this. The caller MUST guarantee `out_sig_ptr` has at least
3309 writable bytes; there is no `out_sig_len` argument to gate on
(unlike `pdxb_sign_superblock`).

---- pdxb_verify_inode_tail(inode_ptr, tail_offset, tail_len, sig_ptr, sig_len, pub_key_slot) -> err
**STUB — fail-closed by construction.** Always returns
`PDXB_VER_ERR_NOT_IMPLEMENTED` and dereferences none of its six
arguments. No `mldsa65_verify` intrinsic exists in paideia-as v0.24.0
(repo-wide grep across paideia-os and its paideia-as submodule came
back empty). See [[cref: LIMITATIONS]].

==== WIRE-FORMATS

---- PdxbSuperblockSummary (in-memory decoded struct, 176 bytes / 22 u64 slots)
Decodes the fixed-field region of the on-disk 4096-byte PDXB v1
superblock (`design/filesystem/volume-fs-substrate.md` §2.1,
paideia-os — authoritative; this library never redefines it). Every
slot is a full aligned `u64` regardless of the on-disk field's real
width, since paideia-as has no native sub-8-byte struct-field
addressing beyond raw byte offsets.

    [  0,  8) magic           (on-disk [0,4),   zero-extended u32)
    [  8, 16) version         (on-disk [4,8),   zero-extended u32)
    [ 16, 24) uuid_lo         (on-disk [8,16),  uuid bytes 0..8)
    [ 24, 32) uuid_hi         (on-disk [16,24), uuid bytes 8..16)
    [ 32, 40) block_size      (on-disk [24,28), zero-extended u32)
    [ 40, 48) flags           (on-disk [28,32), zero-extended u32)
    [ 48, 56) total_blocks    (on-disk [32,40))
    [ 56, 64) itable_lba      (on-disk [40,48))
    [ 64, 72) itable_bcount   (on-disk [48,56))
    [ 72, 80) alloc_lba       (on-disk [56,64))
    [ 80, 88) alloc_bcount    (on-disk [64,72))
    [ 88, 96) journal_lba     (on-disk [72,80))
    [ 96,104) journal_bcount  (on-disk [80,88))
    [104,112) data_lba        (on-disk [88,96))
    [112,120) data_bcount     (on-disk [96,104))
    [120,128) root_inode      (on-disk [104,112))
    [128,136) mount_gen       (on-disk [112,120))
    [136,144) snap_head       (on-disk [120,128))
    [144,176) sig_key_hash    (on-disk [128,160), 4 x u64 slots)

Not decoded: on-disk `_reserved` (536 B at offset 160) and `sig`
(3400 B at offset 696, ML-DSA-65 signature covering on-disk `[0,696)`
— this is a SUPERSET of the 176-byte summary above, since it also
covers `_reserved`). `pdxb_sign_superblock` reads directly from the
original on-disk buffer, not from the decoded summary.

---- MountTableRow (in-memory decoded struct, 56 bytes / 7 u64 slots)
Decodes the `KIND_PDXFS_MOUNT_TABLE` singleton capability metadata row
(64 bytes on-wire, `src/kernel/core/cap/kind_pdxfs_mount_table.pdx`
SECTION 1, paideia-os). This is ONE row describing the capability
itself — a pointer to the kernel's `_mount_table[]` array plus a slot
count — NOT one row per active mount.

    [ 0,  8) kind              (header0 bits [15:0]  — must equal 0x1A5)
    [ 8, 16) in_use            (header0 bits [63:56] — 0 or 1)
    [16, 24) flags             (header0 bits [55:32] — 24 bits)
    [24, 32) gen               (header0 bits [31:16])
    [32, 40) mount_slot_count  (header1 bits [15:0]  — informational only)
    [40, 48) reserved_hi       (header1 bits [63:32])
    [48, 56) table_row_addr    (row word 2, verbatim)

`table_row_addr` points at `src/kernel/core/fs/mount.pdx`'s
`_mount_table[MOUNT_MAX=8]` array (R16-M1-005, frozen, 8 bytes/slot),
which `mount_table_snapshot` walks:

    _mount_table[8] per-slot layout (8 bytes/slot):
      [ 0, 16) mountpoint_vnode_idx (u16)
      [16, 32) root_vnode_idx       (u16)
      [32, 40) backend_type         (u8)  NONE=0 TMPFS=1 DEVFS=2
                                            PROCFS=3 TTY=4 PDXFS_BLOCK=5
      [40, 48) flags                (u8)  bit0 VALID bit1 ROOT
                                            bit2 PENDING_UNMOUNT
      [48, 64) _reserved            (u16)

This is NOT the richer `{mount_id, volume_uuid, mount_point_id,
backend_id, flags, mount_gen, invoker_user}` per-mount record
`design/tooling/volume-tooling-ux.md` §2.2 sketches — that record has
no landed kernel representation anywhere in the tree as of v1.0.0. See
[[cref: LIMITATIONS]].

==== LIMITATIONS
Cited from `design/architecture.md`; each item names the section with
the full rationale.

- **`vol_kind_mint` is a permanent stub** until `KIND_VOLUME` gains a
  ring-3-reachable mint syscall (§7).
- **`vol_kind_narrow` does not produce a kernel-enforced narrower
  capability.** `KIND_VOLUME`'s op catalog is query-only (ordinals
  0..9, all `VOL_OP_QUERY_*` plus `VOL_OP_DEBUG_PRINT`); no
  `mount`/`flush`/`snapshot` op exists to narrow to, and no generic
  `cap_narrow` primitive exists anywhere in the kernel tree for this
  KIND (§5, §5.1).
- **`mount_table_row_parse` / `mount_table_snapshot` decode the
  singleton capability metadata row and the live `_mount_table[]`
  vnode-layer array — not the design doc's own §2.2 per-mount-entry
  sketch**, which has no landed kernel representation (no mint path,
  no write op, no field-packing code exists for it anywhere in the
  tree) (§4, §4.3).
- **No on-disk checksum field exists in PDXB v1.** `pdxb_parse_
  superblock` gates on `block_size == 4096` in its place — the closest
  real, mount-time-refusable field the spec defines (§3.1).
- **`_reserved` non-zero forward-compatibility refusal is NOT
  implemented** in the codec — that policy belongs at the mount-time
  caller, not the decode layer (§3.1).
- **Signing helpers take a raw `seed_ptr`, not a `KIND_SIG_KEY` cap
  slot.** `KIND_SIG_KEY`'s landed shape is a PUBLIC-key handle (used
  for mount-time cross-checking), not a private signing-seed store —
  no kernel capability kind anywhere in the tree holds private
  ML-DSA-65 signing-key material. This library also issues zero
  cap-invoke calls by established discipline, so it would not resolve
  such a slot even if one existed (§8.2).
- **`pdxb_verify_inode_tail` is a fail-closed stub.** No
  `mldsa65_verify` intrinsic exists in paideia-as v0.24.0 (§8.4).
- **The dual-signed release manifest is not actually signed at
  v1.0.0.** `release/manifest.pdxsig.txt` ships with every hash and
  signature slot as a documented placeholder — sign-then-push requires
  live release-line key material this repo does not hold, and is a
  release-time step outside this milestone (`design/architecture.md`
  §10).

