==== VERSION
libpdx-volume 1.1.2 (patch on v1.1.1: additive superblock setter
accessors). Closes issue #34 (six new write accessors symmetric to
the existing read accessors on `PdxbSuperblockSummary` in
`src/pdxb_superblock.pdx`: `pdxb_sb_set_itable_lba`,
`pdxb_sb_set_itable_bcount`, `pdxb_sb_set_alloc_lba`,
`pdxb_sb_set_alloc_bcount`, `pdxb_sb_set_journal_lba`,
`pdxb_sb_set_journal_bcount`). Additive source-only change; every
v1.1.1 API surface remains byte-for-byte compatible.

libpdx-volume 1.1.1 (patch on v1.1.0: quota input-contract
clarification + arithmetic-wrap refusal). Closes issues #32 (parameter
rename `quota_row_ptr` → `quota_summary_ptr` on `pdxb_quota_check` /
`pdxb_quota_commit`, plus [[cref: QUOTAS]] documenting the raw-row vs
decoded-summary distinction) and #33 (overflow guard on
`blocks_used + block_delta` inside `pdxb_quota_check`). Source-only
change; ABI byte-identical to v1.1.0.

libpdx-volume 1.1.0 (LV.M1..LV.M6 audit-driven follow-up over the
v1.0.0 R53 wave). Additive minor release closing 16 tickets
(#16..#31); every v1.0.0 API surface is preserved byte-for-byte. See
`CHANGELOG.md`'s 1.1.0 section for the full landing manifest, and
`design/architecture.md` §11 for the wire-format additions
(`_reserved` region reuse, PDXB v2 encryption gating, snap-metadata
records, quota rows, mount-deps blocks). The dual-sign + mirror-push
run remains deferred with the same three external gates as v1.0.0
(paideia-as toolchain in CI, `pkgs.paideia-os` endpoint,
release-line ML-DSA-65 seed key custody) — see
`release/RELEASE-1.0.0.md` §3.

==== V1.1.0 API additions (index)
Full contracts in each module's own header + `design/architecture.md`
§11. Every symbol below is additive on top of v1.0.0.

- **`src/pdxb_checksum.pdx`** — `pdxb_superblock_checksum(sb_ptr,
  buf_len)`, `pdxb_verify_checksum(sb_ptr, expected)`. CRC32C over the
  [0, 696) signed range (real bodies).
- **`src/lpv_errors.pdx`** — `LPV_E_*` banded namespace (VK, MTR,
  MTS, PDXB, SIGN, VER, SNAP, QUOTA, CRYPTO, ORDER, STUB bands);
  `lpv_strerror(code, out, cap)` scaffold (bindings landed; dispatch
  table follow-up).
- **`src/vol_snapshot.pdx`** — `KIND_VOLUME_SNAPSHOT = 0x1A1`;
  `vol_snapshot_narrow` real body (validate + passthrough);
  `vol_snapshot_mint` / `pdxb_snap_create` / `snap_chain_walk` stubs;
  `snap_record_parse` real body over the 96-byte metadata record.
- **`src/pdxb_quota.pdx`** — `PDXQ_MAGIC = 0x50445851`; wire format
  documented; `pdxb_quota_row_parse` / `_row_encode` / `_table_lookup`
  real bodies; `pdxb_quota_check` (4 return codes + BAD_ROW);
  `pdxb_quota_commit` with underflow clamp. Block path fully wired;
  inode path is a follow-up. See [[cref: QUOTAS]] for the layout
  contract shared by `_check` / `_commit`.
- **`src/pdxb_crypto.pdx`** — `KIND_KEK = 0x1A2`; `pdxb_kek_derive`
  (Argon2id RFC 9106 profile); `pdxb_dek_wrap` / `_unwrap` (ChaCha20-
  Poly1305); `pdxb_block_encrypt` / `_decrypt` stubs pending
  paired-block layout.
- **`src/mount_deps.pdx`** — `PDDP_MAGIC = 0x50444450`; per-dep entry
  128 bytes; `mount_deps_parse` real body; `mount_table_sort_by_deps`
  stub pending Kahn's-algorithm body.
- **`src/pdxb_sign.pdx`** additions: `pdxb_verify_superblock` stub
  (blocked on `mldsa65_verify`); `pdxb_sign_superblock_traced`
  (audit_client_slot == 0 fast-path fully working).
- **`src/pdxb_superblock.pdx`** additions: 22 getters + 10 setters
  over `PdxbSuperblockSummary`; `PDXB_ONDISK_BYTES`,
  `PDXB_VERSION_V2`, `PDXB_FLAG_HAS_QUOTA`, `PDXB_FLAG_ENCRYPTED`;
  PDXB v2 wrapped-DEK/salt accessors over `_reserved[+192, +268)`;
  parser accepts v1 or v2.
- **`src/mount_table.pdx`** additions: 7 `MountTableRow` field
  getters (`mtr_get_kind` through `mtr_get_table_row_addr`).
- **`src/mount_table_snapshot.pdx`** additions: 5 `MountTableEntry`
  field getters (`mte_get_mountpoint_vnode_idx` through
  `mte_get_reserved`); `MTE_BYTES = 40` alias.
- **`src/vol_kind.pdx`** additions: `vol_kind_mint_elevate(dev_cap,
  elevate_channel_slot, out_slot)` — 3-arg elevate-aware form; body
  stubs pending kernel-side mint syscall + libpdx-elevate link.

==== QUOTAS
The quota subsystem exposes two on-wire layouts that a caller MUST
NOT confuse. Both `pdxb_quota_check` and `pdxb_quota_commit` (v1.1.1,
issue #32) operate on the DECODED summary layout, not on the raw
on-disk row; their first parameter is named `quota_summary_ptr` to
make this unambiguous at every call site.

---- Two layouts, two offset families

**Raw on-disk row** (64 bytes, packed) — the wire format `mkfs.pdxfs`
writes to the quota-table blocks and `pdxb_quota_row_parse` /
`pdxb_quota_row_encode` read/write. Field offsets are the
`PDXQ_D_OFF_*` family:

    [+0]   magic         (u32,  PDXQ_D_OFF_MAGIC           = 0)
    [+4]   version       (u16,  PDXQ_D_OFF_VERSION         = 4)
    [+6]   subject_kind  (u8,   PDXQ_D_OFF_SUBJECT_KIND    = 6)
    [+8]   subject_id_lo (u64,  PDXQ_D_OFF_SUBJECT_ID_LO   = 8)
    [+16]  subject_id_hi (u64,  PDXQ_D_OFF_SUBJECT_ID_HI   = 16)
    [+24]  blocks_used   (u64,  PDXQ_D_OFF_BLOCKS_USED     = 24)
    [+32]  blocks_soft   (u64,  PDXQ_D_OFF_BLOCKS_SOFT     = 32)
    [+40]  blocks_hard   (u64,  PDXQ_D_OFF_BLOCKS_HARD     = 40)
    [+48]  inodes_used   (u64,  PDXQ_D_OFF_INODES_USED     = 48)
    [+56]  inodes_soft_hard  (packed u64,
                              PDXQ_D_OFF_INODES_SOFT_HARD  = 56)

**Decoded summary** (88 bytes, 11 aligned u64 slots) — the in-memory
form `pdxb_quota_row_parse` writes to `out_ptr` and every enforcement
helper reads. Field offsets are the `PDXQ_OFF_*` family:

    [+0]   magic         (PDXQ_OFF_MAGIC          = 0)
    [+8]   version       (PDXQ_OFF_VERSION        = 8)
    [+16]  subject_kind  (PDXQ_OFF_SUBJECT_KIND   = 16)
    [+24]  subject_id_lo (PDXQ_OFF_SUBJECT_ID_LO  = 24)
    [+32]  subject_id_hi (PDXQ_OFF_SUBJECT_ID_HI  = 32)
    [+40]  blocks_used   (PDXQ_OFF_BLOCKS_USED    = 40)
    [+48]  blocks_soft   (PDXQ_OFF_BLOCKS_SOFT    = 48)
    [+56]  blocks_hard   (PDXQ_OFF_BLOCKS_HARD    = 56)
    [+64]  inodes_used   (PDXQ_OFF_INODES_USED    = 64)
    [+72]  inodes_soft   (PDXQ_OFF_INODES_SOFT    = 72,
                          decoded high half of inodes_soft_hard)
    [+80]  inodes_hard   (PDXQ_OFF_INODES_HARD    = 80,
                          decoded low half of inodes_soft_hard)

The layouts share none of their non-magic offsets. `blocks_used`, for
example, is at +24 on disk and +40 in the summary. Passing a raw
on-disk row directly to `pdxb_quota_check` or `pdxb_quota_commit` is a
silent-mismatch bug: the `mov_d` (u32) magic gate at `+0` still observes
`PDXQ_MAGIC` by accident, so the BAD_ROW gate does NOT fire; the
helper then reads blocks_used from what is really the packed
inodes_used/inodes_soft_hard region and emits a nonsense verdict.

---- Compose parse → check → commit

    // Raw on-disk row (64 bytes) came from a block read.
    let mut summary : [u8; 88]   // PDXQ_SUMMARY_BYTES
    let rc = pdxb_quota_row_parse(raw_row_ptr, &summary)
    if rc != 0 { return rc }     // BAD_ROW etc.

    // Enforcement helpers take the DECODED summary, not the raw row.
    let check_rc = pdxb_quota_check(&summary,
                                    block_delta,
                                    inode_delta,
                                    grace_expired)
    if check_rc == LPV_QUOTA_HARD_EXCEEDED
       || check_rc == LPV_QUOTA_SOFT_GRACE_EXPIRED { return check_rc }

    // Apply the delta (underflow clamped, arithmetic wrap refused
    // upstream in _check).
    pdxb_quota_commit(&summary, block_delta, inode_delta)

    // To persist, re-encode the mutated summary back to the on-disk
    // row and write it through the block device.
    pdxb_quota_row_encode(&summary, raw_row_ptr)

The v1.1.1 rename from `quota_row_ptr` to `quota_summary_ptr` is
source-only: no ABI or offset shift, and existing v1.1.0 callers keep
compiling. `pdxb_quota_check` additionally refuses raw-arithmetic
wrap on `blocks_used + block_delta` with `LPV_QUOTA_HARD_EXCEEDED`
(issue #33), matching the defensive posture
`kernel/core/syscall/ptr_check.pdx` uses for `va + len` overflow.
